WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:01.280
- [Instructor] We're asked to prove

00:01.280 --> 00:04.700
that if a line is parallel
to one side of a triangle,

00:04.700 --> 00:09.120
then it divides the other
two sides proportionally.

00:09.120 --> 00:11.040
So pause this video and
see if you can do that.

00:11.040 --> 00:13.223
And you might wanna leverage this diagram.

00:14.600 --> 00:16.810
All right, so let's work
through this together.

00:16.810 --> 00:18.780
So we can start with this diagram.

00:18.780 --> 00:19.940
And what we know

00:19.940 --> 00:24.300
is that segment ED is
parallel to segment CB.

00:24.300 --> 00:25.540
So we can write that down.

00:25.540 --> 00:30.540
Segment ED is parallel to segment CB.

00:33.190 --> 00:36.510
And so segment ED is what
they're talking about.

00:36.510 --> 00:38.150
That is a line or a line segment

00:38.150 --> 00:40.600
that is parallel to one
side of the triangle.

00:40.600 --> 00:42.360
So really given what we know,

00:42.360 --> 00:45.190
and what's already been written
over here on this triangle,

00:45.190 --> 00:47.897
we need to prove another
way of writing it,

00:47.897 --> 00:50.130
another way of saying it divides

00:50.130 --> 00:52.110
the other two sides proportionately,

00:52.110 --> 00:53.620
is that the ratio

00:53.620 --> 00:56.590
between the part of the
original triangle side

00:56.590 --> 00:58.710
that is on one side of the dividing line

00:58.710 --> 01:00.950
to the length on the other side

01:00.950 --> 01:03.310
is going to be the same on both sides

01:03.310 --> 01:04.400
that it is intersecting.

01:04.400 --> 01:05.880
So another way to say

01:05.880 --> 01:08.510
that it divides the other
two sides proportionately,

01:08.510 --> 01:10.340
if we look at this triangle over here,

01:10.340 --> 01:12.780
it would mean that the
length of segment AE

01:14.520 --> 01:16.590
over the length of segment EC

01:18.350 --> 01:20.830
is going to be equal to
the length of segment AD

01:22.820 --> 01:25.373
over the length of segment DB.

01:26.770 --> 01:27.960
This statement right over here,

01:27.960 --> 01:29.800
and what I underlined up here

01:29.800 --> 01:32.600
are equivalent given this triangle.

01:32.600 --> 01:34.640
So the way that we can try to do it

01:34.640 --> 01:36.830
is to establish a similarity

01:36.830 --> 01:41.830
between triangle AED and triangle ACB.

01:42.050 --> 01:43.850
So how do we do that?

01:43.850 --> 01:47.080
Well, because these
two lines are parallel,

01:47.080 --> 01:49.580
we can view segment AC

01:49.580 --> 01:52.440
as a transversal intersecting
two parallel lines.

01:52.440 --> 01:55.090
So that tells us that these
two corresponding angles

01:55.090 --> 01:57.040
are going to be congruent.

01:57.040 --> 02:02.040
So we could say that angle one
is congruent to angle three.

02:04.620 --> 02:05.970
And the reason why,

02:05.970 --> 02:10.893
is because they are corresponding,
corresponding angles.

02:12.190 --> 02:14.010
I'm just trying to write
a little bit of shorthand.

02:14.010 --> 02:16.370
This is short for corresponding angles.

02:16.370 --> 02:17.910
That's the rationale.

02:17.910 --> 02:19.820
And we also know that angle two

02:19.820 --> 02:22.650
is congruent to angle
four for the same reason.

02:22.650 --> 02:27.650
So angle two is congruent to angle four.

02:28.040 --> 02:31.450
Once again, because they
are corresponding angles.

02:31.450 --> 02:33.850
This time we have a different transversal,

02:33.850 --> 02:34.870
corresponding angles

02:34.870 --> 02:37.860
where a transversal
intersects two parallel lines.

02:37.860 --> 02:42.580
And so now, if you look at
triangle AED and triangle ACB,

02:42.580 --> 02:46.550
you see that they have two
sets of corresponding angles

02:46.550 --> 02:47.383
that are congruent.

02:47.383 --> 02:49.000
And if you have two sets
of corresponding angles,

02:49.000 --> 02:50.890
that means that all of
the angles are congruent.

02:50.890 --> 02:52.780
And you actually see that over
here, if you care about it,

02:52.780 --> 02:55.240
but two is enough, but
you actually have a third

02:55.240 --> 02:57.290
because angle, I guess you call it BAC

02:58.150 --> 03:00.000
is common to both triangles.

03:00.000 --> 03:02.710
And so we can say that triangle AED

03:05.683 --> 03:08.357
is similar to triangle ACB,

03:09.669 --> 03:14.669
ACB by angle similarity.

03:15.400 --> 03:16.233
Similarity.

03:17.460 --> 03:20.210
And then given that these two are similar,

03:20.210 --> 03:22.370
then we can set up a proportion.

03:22.370 --> 03:26.900
That tells us that the ratio
of the length of segment AE

03:28.320 --> 03:31.673
to this entire side to AC,

03:33.560 --> 03:38.560
is equal to the ratio of AD,
the length of that segment

03:39.650 --> 03:44.260
to the length of the entire thing, to AB.

03:44.260 --> 03:47.100
Now this implies, and I'm
just gonna start writing it

03:47.100 --> 03:48.990
to the right here to save space.

03:48.990 --> 03:52.750
This is the same thing
as the ratio of AE over,

03:52.750 --> 03:56.720
AC is AE plus EC's length.

03:56.720 --> 04:01.720
So AE's length plus EC's length,

04:01.860 --> 04:03.650
and then this is going to be equal

04:03.650 --> 04:05.600
to the length of segment AD

04:05.600 --> 04:10.503
over segment AB, its length
is the length of segment AD,

04:11.590 --> 04:16.590
AD plus segment DB, plus D B.

04:16.950 --> 04:18.170
Now, really what I need to do

04:18.170 --> 04:20.700
is figure out how do I
algebraically manipulate it

04:20.700 --> 04:23.840
so I get what I have up here.

04:23.840 --> 04:26.200
Let me scroll down a little bit.

04:26.200 --> 04:28.140
So one way I could try to simplify this

04:28.140 --> 04:30.490
is to essentially cross multiply,

04:30.490 --> 04:32.760
that's equivalent to
multiplying both sides

04:32.760 --> 04:34.590
by both of these denominators.

04:34.590 --> 04:36.080
And we've covered that in other videos.

04:36.080 --> 04:39.780
And so this is going to be equal
to the length of segment AE

04:39.780 --> 04:44.780
times AD plus DB, those segment lengths,

04:45.090 --> 04:49.290
that's gotta be equal
to length of AD times AE

04:52.090 --> 04:55.380
plus the length of segment EC.

04:55.380 --> 04:57.480
And I can distribute this over here.

04:57.480 --> 05:01.410
I have length of segment AE
times length of segment AD

05:02.298 --> 05:06.631
plus length of segment AE
times length of segment DB

05:08.751 --> 05:13.242
is equal to length of segment
AD times length of segment AE

05:13.242 --> 05:17.659
plus length of segment AD
times length of segment EC.

05:18.710 --> 05:21.390
And let's see, is there anything
that I can simplify here?

05:21.390 --> 05:25.200
We'll have AE times AD on both sides.

05:25.200 --> 05:29.550
So let me just subtract AE
times AD from both sides.

05:29.550 --> 05:33.340
And so then I'm just left
with this is equal to that.

05:33.340 --> 05:36.410
So scroll down a little bit more

05:36.410 --> 05:38.740
and let me actually just
rewrite this cleanly.

05:38.740 --> 05:43.740
So I have AE times DB
is equal to AD times EC.

05:46.470 --> 05:48.500
These are all the segment
lengths right over here.

05:48.500 --> 05:51.260
Now, if you divide both sides by EC,

05:51.260 --> 05:54.070
you're going to get an EC down here,

05:54.070 --> 05:55.520
and then this would cancel out.

05:55.520 --> 05:58.130
And then if you divide both sides by DB,

05:58.130 --> 06:01.660
this will cancel out and you'll
get a DB right over here.

06:01.660 --> 06:03.350
So if you just algebraically manipulate

06:03.350 --> 06:04.820
what we just had over there,

06:04.820 --> 06:07.020
you get that the length of segment AE

06:07.020 --> 06:08.700
over the length of segment EC,

06:08.700 --> 06:12.660
length of segment AE over
the length of segment EC

06:12.660 --> 06:15.043
is equal to the length of segment AD, AD

06:18.290 --> 06:22.750
over the length of segment DB,

06:22.750 --> 06:24.860
which is exactly what we wanted to prove.

06:24.860 --> 06:26.200
That this line right over here

06:26.200 --> 06:28.600
that is parallel to this side over here,

06:28.600 --> 06:31.483
divides the other two
sides proportionally.
